feat: site-wide meta descriptions + OpenGraph tags + dynamic OG image

- app/opengraph-image.tsx (new): 1200x630 wordmark on emerald gradient,
  served at /opengraph-image, auto-linked into every page's <head>
- app/layout.tsx: removed broken /og-image.png reference (file never
  existed); updated site default description + title

Per-page descriptions matched to user-supplied SEO copy where given;
existing per-page descriptions preserved otherwise. Every page now has
both meta description and explicit openGraph.title/description so
sharing previews match search snippets:

  /about, /how-it-works, /tools, /contact, /privacy, /terms, /blog,
  /pricing, /hvac, /plumbing, /electrical, /roofing,
  /features/{ai-receptionist, content-creation, lead-scoring,
  review-management, website-optimization}

Blog routes:
- 5 MDX files renamed to longer SEO-friendly slugs matching user list
- Each frontmatter excerpt replaced with user's punchier copy (excerpts
  feed both index cards + meta descriptions via generateMetadata)
- app/blog/[slug]/page.tsx: generateMetadata now sets openGraph too
- app/sitemap.ts: URLs updated to match renamed slugs

Pricing refactor: app/pricing/page.tsx was "use client" which blocks
metadata export. Renamed to PricingClient.tsx; new page.tsx is a thin
server component exporting metadata + rendering PricingClient.

